19. Mixing .l syntax and raw C
------------------------------

#linux

int main()
    counter = 3
    printf("raw printf call with normal C syntax\n");
    int explicit_value = 42

    if counter > 0:
        print("counter is positive")
        puts("raw C call can be used inside a block")

    return 0

Tip: typed C declarations and common raw C calls can be mixed with .l syntax.
For complex raw C, keep complete C syntax.


20. Passing gcc options
-----------------------

Compile with warnings:

./compilateur main.l -Wall -Wextra -o app

Compile with the math library:

./compilateur main.l -lm -o app

Translate only and keep the generated C:

./compilateur main.l -without-binary -keep_c

Translate a header only and keep the generated header:

./compilateur api.H -without-binary -keep_h


21. Complete program
--------------------

Source: demo.l

#all
#linux

int square(int x)
    return x * x

int sum_until(int n)
    total = 0
    for i in range(n):
        total = total + i
    return total

int main()
    name = "Ada"
    limit = 5
    total = sum_until(limit)
    square_of_four = square(4)

    print("Hello {name}")
    print("sum before {limit} = {total}")
    print("square of 4 = {square_of_four}")

    values = [10, 20, 30]
    head::tail = values
    print("first={head}, remaining={tail_len}")

    match total with
        | 0 -> print("zero")
        | _ if total > 5 -> print("greater than five")
        | _ -> print("small total")

    match values with
        | [] -> print("no values")
        | [x] -> print("one value {x}")
        | head2::tail2 -> print("several values, first={head2}")

    return 0

Recommended command for learning:

./compilateur demo.l -without-binary -keep_c

Then open demo.c and compare it with demo.l.


22. Common errors
-----------------

Invalid identifier:

int main()
    123bad = 10
    return 0

Mixed list types:

int main()
    mixed = [1, 2.5, "text"]
    return 0

Malformed list decomposition:

int main()
    values = [1, 2, 3]
    head:: = values
    return 0

Malformed match:

int main()
    match with
        | 1 -> print("bad")
    return 0

Malformed print interpolation:

int main()
    value = 10
    print("value={value")
    return 0

Empty print interpolation:

int main()
    print("value={}")
    return 0
